    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 7.4,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.97,
    "rationale": "Undiluted readings flatten at about 2.0 from 8 h onward, right after fast exponential growth. That pattern points to the reader saturating, not to growth stopping. I diluted the 18 h aliquot 10× and got 0.727 (0.7243 and 0.7294), which scales to about 7.3. A 40× dilution gave 0.186 (0.1867 and 0.1857), which scales to about 7.4. The two dilutions agree after scaling, so the reader responds proportionally at these lower readings. Both scaled values are far above the undiluted 2.0, so the true biomass at 18 h is about OD 7.4, not 2.0. I only measured the 18 h aliquot directly. The flat undiluted readings from 8 h onward suggest the same underestimate applies to the other late hours."
  },
